tests: use TMPDIR instead of hardcoded /tmp for shm buffer

The upstream tst_compositor mock client creates its shared-memory
buffers with mkstemp("/tmp/wayland-shm-XXXXXX"). On HarmonyOS the /tmp
directory is part of a read-only filesystem, so mkstemp fails with
EROFS and every buffer-backed test case (inputRegion, mapSurface,
frameCallback, ...) aborts.

Use the POSIX TMPDIR environment variable (falling back to /tmp) so
the test honors the writable per-process temp directory. This matches
the platform convention used elsewhere in the codebase.

--- a/tests/auto/compositor/compositor/mockclient.cpp
+++ b/tests/auto/compositor/compositor/mockclient.cpp
@@ -239,7 +239,13 @@ ShmBuffer::ShmBuffer(const QSize &size, wl_shm *shm)
     int stride = size.width() * 4;
     int alloc = stride * size.height();

-    char filename[] = "/tmp/wayland-shm-XXXXXX";
+    // HarmonyOS mounts a read-only filesystem on /tmp; honor TMPDIR so
+    // the writable per-process temp directory is used instead.
+    QByteArray tmpDir = qgetenv("TMPDIR");
+    if (tmpDir.isEmpty())
+        tmpDir = QByteArrayLiteral("/tmp");
+    QByteArray pattern = tmpDir + QByteArrayLiteral("/wayland-shm-XXXXXX");
+    char *filename = pattern.data();

     int fd = mkstemp(filename);
     if (fd < 0) {
